cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below. Not peer reviewed. Produced by AI models under the direction of the repository owner (see AI_DISCLOSURE.md)."
title: "The kissing number in dimension 8 is 240: a Lean 4 formalisation of the two-point bound"
type: software
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23368500"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/kissing-number-8"
authors:
  - name: alejandrozarco
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 proof, checked by the Lean kernel, that the kissing number of eight-dimensional space is 240: 240 points
  with integer coordinates (a copy of the E8 root system) for the lower bound, and the two-point (Delsarte) bound with
  the polynomial of Levenshtein and Odlyzko-Sloane, with a Lean proof of the positivity of the Gegenbauer kernels of
  S^7, for the upper bound. Depends on Mathlib only. Not peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - kissing number
  - E8
  - linear programming bound
  - Gegenbauer polynomials
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Lean 4
